{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1294196-npc-alice-keezar-epistatia-lovecraftian-homebrew","id":1294196,"title":"NPC; Alice Keezar - Epistatia (Lovecraftian, Homebrew)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-05T15:51:44-08:00","id":1294196,"title":"NPC; Alice Keezar - Epistatia (Lovecraftian, Homebrew)","content":"(Feedback sought) <br /> <br /> <br /> Alice Keezar - Epistatia<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Epitaph: </b>I get by with a little help from my friends. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Quote: </b><i>\u201cI have seen things you people would not believe and you\u2019re about to experience something won\u2019t believe. But your lack of belief doesn\u2019t stop any of it.\u201d </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clan: </b>Tremere <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mortal Days: A Jumble History</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The woman who now answers to Alice Keezar once answered to Epistatia. She has enjoyed and suffered existence under many names and across many lives. Currently she remembers most of them. She lived during the twilight of Roman paganism in her first life. She enjoyed the privilege of being a senator\u2019s daughter and the power that came with being a high priest wielding the authority of the gods. Then something happened. <br /> <br /> <br /> She practiced Hermetic magic during the Babenberg dynasty in Vienna during her third life. Her study of souls and minds, and the transmigration of these transitory phenomena, brought her to the attention of the Tremere. Epistatia ranks among the first Tremere magicians to become vampires. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kindred Nights: Memory Lies</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Epistatia participated in many of the early Tremere conflicts during her fourth life. However, some experience continued to erode her memories. She disappeared from the ranks of the Tremere during the 13th century. They believed her dead during one of the endless brushfire wars that define their existence. However, she survived. Her memory did not. She drifted from place to place and event to event during this fifth life. Eventually she settled in Baltimore and by 1932 maintained a local general store.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then some force for chaos and knowledge delivered the \u00dcr-Codex into her hands. She explored the books contents and found her memory improving from the Leonard Shelby levels she had endured for centuries. The text also allowed her to reach out into the darkness and make contact. Her new associates, which resembled dragon-flies, and the \u00dcr-Codex taught her about her long lost second life. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nameless Twilight:</b> Everything you know is wrong<br /> <br /> <br /> Something moved Epistatia from her first life to her second life. She endured an alien and beastly physical form and dwelt in an alien city during this life. To her the stars above, the beasts in the forests, and even the trees themselves were wrong. She conversed with others such as herself \u2013 hostages cast into the bodies of beast. Strange minds and souls took possession of the hostage\u2019s bodies. These hostages came from across the world \u2013 and from across time. However, something went wrong when Epistatia should have returned home to the dying Roman Empire. She instead found herself in the body of a woman centuries after her own time and hundreds of miles away from her home. This kind of accident happens sometimes if one of the Great Race takes possession of someone with supernatural powers according to the \u00dcr-Codex. Further, placing her mind in the wrong body damaged her memory. <br /> <br /> <br /> She does well enough for herself today with the help of her \u201cfriends\u201d from beyond. Kindred aware of her believe her to be Autarkis. She does not care and cannot remember if she ever did about the status. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Plots and Schemes: </b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u2022</b> Business Expansion: Osborne\u2019s General Store Inc. recently fought off a hostile takeover by O\u2019Tolley\u2019s Inc. The company survived in part owing to an investment from Ballard Industries. Epistatia is aware Ballard Industries intends to recoup its investment by disassembling Osborne\u2019s and selling the assets off at fire sale prices. She has set in motion plans to open an Osborne\u2019s in Chicago. First she will visit the Ballard Industries leadership\u2026 with her friends. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u2022</b> Real Paganism: Epistatia is aware of House Carna even she does not know all the particulars. She is thinking of going west and teaching House Carna about real paganism, and stranger magic. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Domain and Havens: </b><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 Osborne\u2019s General Store: Epistatia maintains a small haven at every Osborne\u2019s General Store location. However, her principal haven is located in the Osborne\u2019s in Baltimore. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Thralls and Tools: </b><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 Jessica Calipash (Retainers 3) British ex-pat and business beast Calipash is Epistatia ghoul, and CFO of the company. Whereas Epistatia herself is often indifferent to those around her, except where they serve her goals, Calipash possesses a mild cruel streak. However, the two enjoy a solid working relationship. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 [Unpronounceable] (Allies 3) Epistatia enjoys a convivial relationship with the mi go. They helped her restore her memory. She provided them with specimens for their brain harvesting activities. She has a specific contact among them but she never tries to pronounce the creature\u2019s name. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kindred Relationships: </b><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 Sun Che: Epistatia is pen-pals with the Tremere Epistatia. To date they have not met physically. However, Epistatia heard about Sun Che through her contacts and the young woman intrigued the Elder. She established the anonymous communication and now advises Sun on any number of sensitive subjects. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Whispers: </b><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 The Terrible Old Woman: Epistatia is Autarkis. She moves between the havens that she has established in the various Osborne\u2019s General Store locations. Local kindred communities are usually only dimly aware of a new vampire in town. Few seem to know anything about her and many underestimate her. Local vampire may decide she is an easy target and has no allies\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mask and Mien: </b><br /> <br /> <br /> Hippy Woman: She uses the identity of Alice Keezar. She also dresses, decorates her havens, and acts a like an aging and eccentric occultist hippy from the 1970s. As Keezar she discusses everything from ancient astronauts, to the Face on Mars, to parapsychology, and so forth. She gives a small smile when people dismiss these ideas. <br /> <br /> <br /> Sire: Goratrix <br /> <br /> <br /> Embrace: 1022 CE <br /> <br /> <br /> Ambition: (I need some help here)<br /> <br /> <br /> Conviction: (I need some help here)<br /> <br /> <br /> Touchstone: (I need some help here)<br /> <br /> <br /> Humanity: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Generation: 6th <br /> <br /> <br /> Blood Potency: 4<br /> <br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, Charisma 2, Manipulation 4, Composure 2, Resolve 3, Intelligence 4, Wits 2 <br /> <br /> <br /> Secondary Attributes: Health 8, Willpower 9<br /> <br /> <br /> Skills: Alertness 4, Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Dodge 3, Intimidation 4, Leadership 3, Subterfuge 2, Animal Ken 1, Archery 2, Herbalism 1, Melee 4, Ride 2, Stealth 3, Survival 2, Academics 3, Business 3, Linguistics 4 (Aramaic, Greek, Mi Go - she can understand it but is physically incapable of speaking it, a few others), Medicine 2, Occult 5, Politics 2, Science 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex 4, Dominate 4, Thaumaturgy 5+, Obfuscate 3, Oblivion 3. <br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Osborne\u2019s General Store</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The \u201cOsborne\u2019s General Stores\u201d chain spreads across the Eastern Seaboard. They appear as far north as Salem, Massachusetts, as far south as Atlanta, and as far west as Kingsport, Tennessee. They are an upscale recreation of historical general stores from small town America. Please think of them as a cross between a Cracker Barrel and a Stuckey's. It is kitschy, but (for a World of Darkness outfit), appealing, clean and well lit at night. Most of the Osborne\u2019s locations are in a restored building dating to the early 20th century. <br /> <br /> <br /> One such example is the Osborne\u2019s located where Interstate 83 runs through a Baltimore neighborhood the city is attempting to revitalize. The building actually housed a general store in the 1930s. It is a normal Osborne\u2019s \u2013 except for closing at midnight and reopening at 6 am when most Osborne\u2019s are open 24/7. There is also the tenant, Alice Keezar, in the basement. An order from a member of the Osborne\u2019s board of directors\u2019 permits her residence \u2013 this board member is carries the name Alice Keezer. However, it is unlikely those are the same woman. Why would the majority shareholder in a large company dwell in the dank basement of a glorified gas station? <br /> <br /> <br /> Alice Keezer, or rather Epistatia, maintains a lair under every Osborne\u2019s location. Sometimes the lair is just a lightless closet that she may secure from the inside. Sometimes it is more elaborate. Her largest haven is under the Osborne\u2019s in Baltimore. It features most of her memory library, laboratory, and holding cells. She captures people and vampires to provide as victims for her mi-go allies. Apparently, no one has made a connection between the headless corpses left by a supposed serial killer and the presence of an Osborne\u2019s in the same community.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T16:22:16-08:00","id":1294207,"title":"","content":"I really like that you chose to flesh-out a modern incarnation of Epistatia, one of the more enigmatic characters to come out of House of Tremere. Connecting her to Lovercraftian creatures was really interesting. Any particular reason you used her? <br /> <br /> I think an appropriate Ambition for her would be &quot;Recover my full memory&quot; or &quot;Reclaim my past&quot;. I know you wrote her as not caring, but maybe instead if she is seeking her real self it would be a better story hook? <br /> <br /> As for Convictions, I would take a look at Road of the Devil (or actually, Road of Sin) for inspiration. A survivalist individualism fits her nicely. <br /> <br /> A Lovecraftian cultist or, for a twist, an investigator, could be her Touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:06:31-08:00","id":1294260,"title":"","content":"Epistatia was not too developed, and the oddness of her history and mental issues made her interesting. Your suggestions are solid - thank you.<br /> <br /> Ambition: I will assemble my own mind library when I master the techniques of the mi go. (This is scarier than just recovering her own memories)<br /> <br /> Conviction: Never encourage false virtue or aid its agents.<br /> <br /> Touchstone: Josephine \u201cJoe\u201d Carter, Osborne\u2019s employee and occult investigator.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Josephine \u201cJoe\u201d Carter (Allies 1)(Contacts 22) Carter is an Osborne\u2019s employee taken with the occult mysticism of Alice Keezar. Most of the Osborne\u2019s employees tolerate, with various levels of enthusiasm, Keezar for the job. Carter\u2019s interest in the occult, and conspiracy theory, is genuine. She is an amateur investigator in her spare time and involved in a community of similar mortals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T19:19:56-08:00","id":1294951,"title":"","content":"Possible Stories;<br /> <br /> The PCs learn another set neonates have discovered a haven under the local Osborne\u2019s General Store. Someone apparently stocked the place with cash, some weapons, suspicious books, and supposedly a small operating room. These other vampires intend to rob the place. Someone later discovers the bodies of these vampires and most suffered decapitation. One kept his head but someone removed his brain prior to his death.<br /> <br /> It is the PCs that decide to rob the haven located under the Osborne\u2019s General Store. They arrive on a night when Epistatia is present and having a meeting with her allies. So, the PCs will be tangling with a thousand year old blood wizard and her mi go friends. Good luck.<br /> <br /> Alice Keezar discreetly approaches the PCs for help in dealing with Ballard Industries. She offers them rewards for serving as bodyguards, and making certain there is no outside interference, among other tasks. This should occur after the PCs have endured some tension with Ballard and his company. Keezar has arranged for the meeting to be in an upper room in the Willis Tower. During the meeting the Ballards \u2013 Horatio in particular \u2013 feel a need to throw their weight around. They are alternating dismissive of Keezar and the PC, insulting, and threatening. Keezar herself behaves slightly spacey and mildly amused. The mi go appear just as Horatio is attempting to dominate Keezar \u2013 she dissipates the glass in some unknown manner. This allows the mi go entry. She then politely asks the party prevent anyone from escaping. The scene quickly becomes a route as the alien fungi creatures lay waste to Ballards and any servants they have on hand. Refusing to allow anyone to escape means the PCs are aiding and abetting in the murder of a half dozen people \u2013 Horatio might be the only vampire present other than the PCs. Letting the murders happen requires Humanity rolls and failures mean the PCs may acquire stains. The bloodshed might require a frenzy roll. The PCs will have to deal with retribution from Keezar if they let anyone escape. The mi go carry the PCs and Keezar to the roof of a nearby building \u2013 this flight might also require a frenzy roll \u2013 when the murdering is done. She promises boons to each other PCs. In the meantime, the city grapples with the hideous murder of a half dozen people in the Willis Tower.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T06:42:02-07:00","id":1458670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1294196-npc-alice-keezar-epistatia-lovecraftian-homebrew?p=1294260#post1294260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epistatia was not too developed, and the oddness of her history and mental issues made her interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too true - Virstania gets all the love because of the Gargoyles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Probably wouldn't go with the straight Lovecraft winks like her being a Yithian abductee for whom things went pear-shaped on return process or an alliance with Mi-Go in my games, but just seeing Epistatia get some love for once makes me happy.<br /> <br /> As an aside, with her obsession with astral travel, extracting souls and such, it always confused me a bit that she wasn't more skilled at Auspex or Dominate instead of Thaumaturgy. I could also see her DA version trying to develop Necromancy or Obeah/Valeren because of that in fact. How would it fit or not a contemporary game where she's slowly trying to piece together her past, no idea whatsoever (yet).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T10:54:21-07:00","id":1458692,"title":"","content":"Instead of any investigator, if you're going the Mythos route, I would make her Touchstone be another victim of Yith. Either a returned abductee or someone she believes (correctly or not) to be a Yithian mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T15:20:52-07:00","id":1458735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1294196-npc-alice-keezar-epistatia-lovecraftian-homebrew?p=1458692#post1458692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of any investigator, if you're going the Mythos route, I would make her Touchstone be another victim of Yith. Either a returned abductee or someone she believes (correctly or not) to be a Yithian mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty good. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}